{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3322","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3322","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3322\",\"parent_revision\":\"bc60fcb2437bbbbada527cf715e0a7bf33de7fdf92ccef18189d4252b7f7a112\",\"root_revision\":\"bc60fcb2437bbbbada527cf715e0a7bf33de7fdf92ccef18189d4252b7f7a112\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe feasibility gate in `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` (Criterion 3 \u2014 blast radius check) treats blast radius as a flat sum of Impact Radius rows across all categories, with a fixed \\\"over 20 systems\\\" BLOCKED threshold. This produced a BLOCKED result while working backlog item #3151 in this session, despite that item having RT-ICA verdict READY and Design Intent verdict MISSION_ALIGNED: the count (~67) mixed 2 structural/high-risk files with ~43 already-itemized, near-identical, low-risk prose edits, and the flat count did not distinguish between them.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: The optional `pattern:` row annotation (intended so the gate can re-verify a count live via `rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l` against staleness) is agent-discretionary \u2014 nothing requires impact-analyst to add it \u2014 and even when present, measures string-match occurrence rather than actual change impact, so it may not reliably signal real blast-radius drift.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: The BLOCKED Output Contract's generic \\\"To retry: re-groom the item... then re-run\\\" footer is intended for Criterion 1 (missing `suggested_location`) and the `STALE_GROOM` branch of Criterion 3 (a live-vs-manual count divergence), where re-grooming can genuinely supply missing or refreshed data. It also fires for the flat \\\">20 systems\\\" branch of Criterion 3, even when the count was freshly produced in the same session and is not stale \u2014 in that case re-grooming would not change the outcome, so the retry advice does not resolve that specific block.\\n\\nImpact: a well-groomed, RT-ICA-ready, mission-aligned item stops at the feasibility gate with retry advice that does not apply to the branch that fired, requiring a human to recognize this and improvise rather than the gate itself surfacing a resolution path.\\n\\nRelated: #1135 (staleness detection for Step 3.1) addresses a different mechanism \u2014 drift between groom date and re-use \u2014 not this item's concern (risk-weighting and threshold design within Criterion 3 itself).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"154d0a3b88e3c8c0eec5a01d6c357077d9c36d765d70a140c1b442fc018c8068\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRaDU4A\"}"}